  "annotations": {
    "engagement": "Three solution tiers gated by read mechanism: Good (handheld snapshot reads), Better (+ fixed readers at chokepoints), Best (full store-wide RTLS). Each value lever is gated per tier (Gating Good/Better/Best) because continuous-dependent value cannot be served by handheld snapshots. Costs are per-store and scale by the 441 in-scope stores. Finance credit (40%) applies to revenue-type levers via the engine's standard rule, matching the workbook's finance-credit column exactly. Accessibility tiers are set per lever on their merits: durable hard-cost visibility (shrink, chargeback) = infrastructure; revenue and labor levers = configured. NPVs are below the workbook's $176.5M-era v4.0 figure because this tool applies conservative ramps with post-peak decay and accessibility compression, which the flat-ramp workbook does not."
  }
